  "name": "Comparing Limits that Do Not Exist",
  "problem": "If two limits *do not exist*, then we *cannot* say that they are equal because we can't compare the undefined values.\n\nSo, if\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x \\to a} f(x) = \\text{DNE}, \\qquad \\lim\\limits_{x \\to b} g(x) = \\text{DNE},\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x \\to a} f(x)  \\neq  \\lim\\limits_{x \\to b} g(x) \\, .\n$$",
